                <pb facs="0792" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13019: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-16T16:00:00+08:00">April 16, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 16—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed by British Consul General that he understands that as a
                    precautionary measure the foreign women and children are being evacuated from
                    Chengtu owing to the danger from communistic attack. Repeat[ed to] the Hankow
                    Consulate General. Repeated to the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
